+   * Handle parallel case robustness: If $P_i P_j$ is nearly horizontal, replace intersection with top edge $Q_T$ with intersection with prolonged right edge $Q_R$ to avoid numerical instability [S1, unofficial].
+   * Handle degenerate edges: If $|x_j - x_i| < \epsilon_I$ and $|y_j - y_i| < \epsilon_I$, assume both vertices are inside $R$ [S1, unofficial]. Check if third vertex $P_k$ is inside $R$ using $x_{min} - \epsilon_I \le x_k \le x_{max} + \epsilon_I$ and $y_{min} - \epsilon_I \le y_k \le y_{max} + \epsilon_I$ [S1, unofficial].
